From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Give the warm reset of the SuperSpeed
 ports 200 ms

warm_reset_usb3_ports() writes WPR into every SuperSpeed port and waits
for the port reset bit to clear, up to 100 ms, then logs an error. With
a device on a port the reset takes longer than that by design: the warm
reset LFPS burst alone lasts 80 to 120 ms by the USB 3.0 specification,
and the receiver detection, the LFPS handshake and the link training
come after it. On a ThinkPad W541 (native raminit) with a USB 3.0 drive
in U3 at every S3 resume the bit is still set at 100 ms, with the port
in Polling, and the port is in U0 about 10 ms later: the error line is
in the log of every resume, for a reset that completes right after the
code stops looking.

Wait up to 200 ms. An empty port clears the bit within microseconds, so
the limit changes nothing there; with a device the wait ends when the
reset does, about 10 ms after the old limit on this machine, and the
rest of romstage finds the port linked.

TEST=ThinkPad W541 (nri): with prints around the reset, at an S3 resume
with a SanDisk Ultra Flair in a USB 3.0 port, PORTSC goes from U3
(0x1263) to Polling with PR set (0x12f1) at 100 ms and to U0 with WRC
and PRC (0x281203) about 10 ms later; at a warm boot the six ports clear
PR in 5 us.
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
index ff167fa1..7861c8b1 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
@@ -248,6 +248,16 @@ static bool reset_usb2_ports(const unsigned int ehci_ports)
 	return !reg32;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The warm reset of a port with a device on it lasts more than 100 ms: the
+ * LFPS burst alone is 80 to 120 ms by the USB 3.0 specification, and the
+ * receiver detection, the LFPS handshake and the link training follow. On
+ * a ThinkPad W541 with a drive in U3 at an S3 resume, the port reset bit
+ * stays set past 100 ms and the port is in U0 about 10 ms later. An empty
+ * port clears the bit at once, so the limit costs nothing there.
+ */
+#define USB3_WARM_RESET_TIMEOUT_MS	200
+
 /* Returns whether warm reset was successful */
 static bool warm_reset_usb3_ports(const unsigned int xhci_ports)
 {
@@ -258,9 +268,9 @@ static bool warm_reset_usb3_ports(const unsigned int xhci_ports)
 			XHCI_USB3_PORTSC_PED,
 			XHCI_USB3_PORTSC_WPR);
 	}
-	/* Poll for port reset bit to be cleared or time out at 100ms */
+	/* Poll for port reset bit to be cleared or time out */
 	struct stopwatch timer;
-	stopwatch_init_msecs_expire(&timer, 100);
+	stopwatch_init_msecs_expire(&timer, USB3_WARM_RESET_TIMEOUT_MS);
 	uint32_t reg32;
 	do {
 		reg32 = 0;
-- 
2.43.0

